r,r-lib/tree-sitter-r,test/corpus/expressions-errors.txt,7,"Dollar, At, Namespace, Namespace Internal With `if` RHS","# The RHS's of these nodes are restricted to strings and identifiers, and the RHS
# is optional. This ends up trying to match to an `if_statement` node, leaving the RHS
# empty, and then the `if_statement` node errors because it doesn't have a `(`. This
# is actually pretty decent behavior.
foo$if
foo@if
foo::if
foo:::if

